Validate the URL to ensure it is within a whitelist of allowed domains. Use a URL parser to check the scheme and host, and reject any URLs that do not match the expected format or domain list. Example:

```java
private static final Set<String> ALLOWED_DOMAINS = Set.of("example.com", "another-example.com");

@GetMapping("/api/preview")
public ResponseEntity<String> preview(@RequestParam String url) {
    URL parsedUrl;
    try {
        parsedUrl = new URL(url);
    } catch (MalformedURLException e) {
        return ResponseEntity.badRequest().body("Invalid URL");
    }

    if (!ALLOWED_DOMAINS.contains(parsedUrl.getHost())) {
        return ResponseEntity.status(HttpStatus.FORBIDDEN).body("URL not allowed");
    }

    String html = http.get().uri(url).retrieve().body(String.class);
    String title = extractTitle(html);
    return ResponseEntity.ok(title);
}
```

